{"id":"word:hebrew:H2319","type":"word","title":"חָדָשׁ","subtitle":"H2319 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"new","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to חָדָשׁ (H2319) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: a.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 53 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"חָדָשׁ (châdâsh) means new First listed occurrence: 1Chr 13 7."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"חָדָשׁ","transliteration":"châdâsh","pronunciation":"khaw-dawsh'","strong":"H2319","lemmaId":"hebrew:H2319","partOfSpeech":"a","forms":["חֲדָשָׁ֔ה","חָדָ֔שׁ","חֲדָשָׁה֙","חָדָ֖שׁ","חֲדָשִׁ֔ים"],"morphs":[["HAamsa",18],["HAafsa",17],["HAampa",10],["HTd/Aafsa",3],["HTd/Aamsa",2],["HC/Aafpa",1],["HAafpa",1],["HTd/Aampa",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"new","usage":"fresh, new thing.","full":"H2319. chadash חָדָשׁ adjective new (on formation see Lg BN 48 ) — ׳ח absolute Exod 1:8 19 t.; feminine חֲדָשָׁה Lev 23:16 19 t.; plural חֲדָשִׁים Deut 32:17 10 t.; feminine חֲדָשׁוֺת Isa 42:9 ; 48:6 ; &#8212; new , usually a. attrib . Exod 1:8 (E) a new king ; so of house Deut 20:5 ; Deuteronomy 20:22, wife 24:5 , cords Judg 15:13 ; 16:11-12 , cart 1Sam 6:7 ; 2Sam 6:3 (twice in verse) (but strike out in v b, compare We Dr) = 1Chr 13:7 , garment 1Kin 11:29-30 , vessel 2Kin 2:20 , wine-skins Josh 9:13 (JE) Job 32:19 , threshing instrument Isaiah 4:15; meal-offering Lev 23:16 (H) Num 28:26 (P); especially (poetry) ח ׳שִׁיר a new song (of praise) Psa 33:3 ; 40:4 ; 96:1 ; 98:1 ; 144:9 ; 149:1 ; Isa 42:10 ; ח ׳בְּרִית Jer 31:31 ; חדשׁה וארץ חדשׁים שָׁמַיִם Isa 65:17 ; compare 66:22 ; ח ׳שֵׁם 62:2 ; ח ׳רוּחַ a new spirit Ezek 11:19 ; 18:31 ; 36:26 , + ח ׳לֵב 18:31 ; 36:26 ; שַׁעַריֿ ׳מֶּתַח ׳הֶח Jer 26:10 new gate of (house of) ׳י , compare 36:10 (see Gf 20:2 ); also הַח ׳הֶחָצֵר 2Chr 20:5 the new court (see Be Öttli); חדשׁים אלהים Judg 5:8 new gods? judges? text probably corrupt, compare Nö ZMG 1888, 477 , Müll Königsb. Stud. i. , GACooke Deb. 34 ff. and conjectures by Bu RS, 103 , RS in Bla Judges ; in General כָּלחֿ ׳אֵין Eccl 1:9 there is nothing new ; with no substantive expressed חֲדָשָׁה חָגוּר 2Sam 21:16 girt with a new (sword: but text perhaps corrupt, compare We Klo Dr), of (food-) products of earth (opposed to יָשָׁן ) Lev 26:10 (H) Cant 7:14; חֲדָשִׁים Deut 32:17 new ones (i.e. gods; || בָּאוּ מִקָּרֹב ); in General feminine חֲדָשָׁה a new thing Isa 43:19 ; Jer 31:22 , feminine plural Isa 42:9 (opposed to הָרִאשֹׁנוֺת ), 48:6 . b. very rarely predicate: of ׳י s compassions לַבְּקָרִם חדשׁים Lam 3:23 they are new every morning ; ח ׳כְּבוֺדִי עִמָּדִי Job 29:20 my glory shall be fresh with me ; ח זֶה ׳רְאֵה הוּא Eccl 1:10 see, this is new! חֲדַ֑ת adjective new ( ᵑ7 Syriac; Biblical Hebrew חדשׁ ); — ׳ח Ezra 6:4 . חוד (√ of following; חוּדִיתָא חוּד, ᵑ7 , riddle , see Biblical Hebrew and K § 57 b ) a)).","rootNote":"from 2318 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 13 7","keyReferences":["1Chr 13 7","1Kgs 11 29","1Kgs 11 30","1Sam 6 7","2Chr 20 5","2Kgs 2 20","2Sam 6 3","2Sam 6 3"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":53,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 13 7","book":"1Chr","chapter":13,"verse":7,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"חֲדָשָׁ֔ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HAafsa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 11 29","book":"1Kgs","chapter":11,"verse":29,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"חֲדָשָׁ֔ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HAafsa"},{"reference":"1Kgs 11 30","book":"1Kgs","chapter":11,"verse":30,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/חֲדָשָׁ֖ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Aafsa"},{"reference":"1Sam 6 7","book":"1Sam","chapter":6,"verse":7,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"חֲדָשָׁה֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HAafsa"},{"reference":"2Chr 20 5","book":"2Chr","chapter":20,"verse":5,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/חֲדָשָֽׁה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Aafsa"},{"reference":"2Kgs 2 20","book":"2